Why each file is here — none is aspirational:
  core_cm0plus.h    included unconditionally by stm32g071xx.h line 115.  There is
                    no way to use the ST device header without it.
  cmsis_version.h   included by core_cm0plus.h line 63.
  cmsis_compiler.h  included by core_cm0plus.h line 115.
  cmsis_gcc.h       selected by cmsis_compiler.h line 54 for __GNUC__ builds.
  mpu_armv7.h       included by core_cm0plus.h line 1007 because stm32g071xx.h
                    sets __MPU_PRESENT 1U.  Verified by deletion: removing this
                    file fails the compile with "mpu_armv7.h: No such file".
                    NeurOne calls no MPU function; the file is a transitive
                    requirement of the device header, not a feature choice.

Intentionally NOT vendored:
  Everything else in CMSIS_5.  Named explicitly so a later reader does not read
  the omissions as oversight:
    CMSIS/DSP/**          CMSIS-DSP — not used by SW-01
    CMSIS/NN/**           CMSIS-NN — not used
    CMSIS/RTOS/**, RTOS2/**  CMSIS-RTOS — SW-01 is bare-metal by design
                          (NP-SW-001 §4.1); SW-02's RTOS is FreeRTOS, vendored
                          separately at firmware/vendor/freertos/
    CMSIS/DAP/**          debug probe firmware — host-side tooling
    CMSIS/Driver/**       peripheral driver API — SW-01 is register-level
    CMSIS/Pack/**, Utilities/**, SVD/**  packaging and tooling
    Core/Include/core_cm{0,3,4,7,23,33,35P,55,85}.h and core_ca*.h,
    core_armv8*.h         other cores; SW-01 is Cortex-M0+ only
    Core/Include/mpu_armv8.h  ARMv8-M MPU; STM32G071 is ARMv7-M
    Core/Include/cmsis_armcc.h, cmsis_armclang*.h, cmsis_iccarm.h,
    cmsis_ccs.h, cmsis_csm.h, tz_context.h
                          other compiler families.  cmsis_compiler.h references
                          them from #elif branches that a __GNUC__ build never
                          takes; NeurOne builds SW-01 with arm-none-eabi-gcc only
                          (firmware/cmake/stm32g071.cmake), so these are
                          unreachable and are deliberately absent rather than
                          carried as unreviewed Class C SOUP surface.

This narrowness is the point, not tidiness.  Every vendored file is Class C SOUP
that has to be justified and anomaly-reviewed (NP-SW-CI-001 §9.4).  Five headers
of register and intrinsic definitions is a materially smaller review burden than
the DSP/NN/RTOS/Driver bodies of logic, and — see the anomaly review — it is also
what makes the §7.1.2 finding as clean as it is: essentially the whole published
anomaly surface of CMSIS_5 lies in components that are not here.
